#EXTM3U
# StreamForge Hub — live playlist (canonical provider references)
#
# WHY THERE ARE NO IP ADDRESSES IN THIS FILE
#   A playlist that hardcodes http://<hub-lan-ip>:8890/... only works on one
#   device, on one network, until DHCP hands out a different lease. It also
#   breaks the moment the same file is imported on a phone, a second TV or a
#   laptop. So this file carries no gateway address at all: every Tivify row is
#   a provider reference (tivify://channel/<code>) that the hub resolves
#   in-process, with no HTTP loopback hop and no assumption about where the
#   gateway lives.
#
#   When the hub exports /live.m3u or /all.m3u it rewrites each reference into a
#   dynamic http://<request-host>:8890/play/<token> link, so whatever address
#   the client used to reach the hub is the address it gets back. External
#   players (TiviMate, IPTVnator, VLC) therefore never see this file — they see
#   the hub's export.
#
#   The #EXTVLCOPT / #KODIPROP hints from the previous revision are gone on
#   purpose: a tivify:// reference is not fetched by the client at all, so the
#   player identity belongs to the hub's own resolver, which injects the TVUp
#   headers server-side (TivifyHttpHeaders.playback()).

# --- Tivify (resolved internally) -------------------------------------------
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="INF70" tvg-name="France 24 English" tvg-logo="" group-title="Tivify",France 24 English
tivify://channel/INF70

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="INF60" tvg-name="France 24 Español" tvg-logo="" group-title="Tivify",France 24 Español
tivify://channel/INF60

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="INF57" tvg-name="Aljazeera English" tvg-logo="" group-title="Tivify",Aljazeera English
tivify://channel/INF57

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="INT36" tvg-name="Aljazeera Arabic" tvg-logo="" group-title="Tivify",Aljazeera Arabic
tivify://channel/INT36

